+\[
+\sum_{t\le T}r_t(a)=a(S_M-1)<p_M(S_M-1)
+=2^{-2M}(2^{M+1}+M-3)\le 1/2.
+\]
+If no such \(M\) exists, the reward is zero. Thus \(\sup_T\sup_a\sum_{t\le T}r_t(a)\le1/2\), and the zero-quote learner has \(O(1)\) regret despite \(\beta(h)\equiv1\).
